 The separately released Objective-C and Swift native sources, their adapted
 third-party notices, and their signing pipeline live in
 `openclaw/openclaw-facetime`.
+
+## Stable audio consent
+
+Runtime setup stages the vendor-signed capture helper at a stable physical path
+in `~/Library/Application Support/OpenClaw/FaceTime/audio`. A small native
+launcher makes that helper its own macOS audio-permission identity, independent
+of Node and Homebrew's versioned installation paths. The helper is not re-signed.
+Setup builds the launcher with the already-required Xcode tools only when its
+source or the installed helper changes. Subsequent starts reuse the staged files.
+
+The launcher replaces its own process, preserving the capture PID, standard
+streams, and shutdown controls. It accepts only capture, `--check`, and
+`--default-devices`; unsupported macOS responsibility APIs fail explicitly.
+Normal macOS consent is still required. A successful process-tap startup is not
+proof of consent or audible audio. Node upgrade and native-helper upgrade
+persistence require separate acceptance checks.
